Award [4 max] 
Double linked list DLL has two external pointers, one pointer points to the first element 
of the DLL, and other points to the last element in the DLL; 
Each node consists of a data field(s); 
and two pointers (for example, called NEXT and PREV); 
Each node is linked with its next node (using its pointer NEXT) and previous node 
(using its pointer PREV); 
The NEXT pointer of the last node is null (to mark the end of the list - forward traversal) 
and the PREV pointer of the first node is null (to mark the end of list - backward 
traversal); 
 Note: Accept diagrams.

