Award [1] for an advantage and [1] mark for an expansion, x2. 
Names can be inserted/deleted quickly/easy just by manipulating the pointers/ by updating 
the address; 
without resorting/shuffling (as in an array);  
Better use of memory/ the number of names (size of the list) is not fixed (as in an array); 
so, no wasted space / linked list can shrink and grow at the runtime (by deallocating or 
allocating memory);  
No need for an initial size/ predetermined size in linked list (as in an array); 
which allocate space that may or may not be fully in use; 
